# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Athena — .gitignore
#  Rule of thumb: commit the STRUCTURE, never the DATA or the SECRETS.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── DATA: application state / preserved knowledge (local only) ──────────────
# Ignore everything under DATA/, but keep the .gitkeep placeholders so the
# directory skeleton survives a clone. (Re-include the dirs first so git can
# descend, then re-include the placeholder files.)
DATA/**
!DATA/**/
!DATA/**/.gitkeep

# Stray DATA/ trees that can appear UNDER INFRASTRUCTURE (runtime artifacts,
# e.g. from running compose with the CWD-relative ./DATA default before the
# ATHENA_DATA_DIR env var was set). These are never canonical — the real data
# lives at the top-level DATA/ dir — so ignore any DATA/ tree nested under
# INFRASTRUCTURE, at any depth.
INFRASTRUCTURE/**/DATA/
INFRASTRUCTURE/**/DATA/**

# ── Secrets & deployment config ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-service .env files hold secrets — never commit them.
# Only the committed .env.example templates are kept.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log

# ── OS / editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
